The draft S-1 submitted on June 1 could not contain these post-filing admissions. Under federal securities law, lead underwriters carry actual notice during the active SEC quiet period. 

3. Securities Act Section 11 Strict Liability (15 U.S.C. Section 77k):
Under Section 11 of the Securities Act of 1933, lead underwriters face joint-and-several strict liability for material omissions in the final public S-1 prospectus. Lead underwriters cannot invoke the statutory "reasonable investigation" due diligence defense under 15 U.S.C. Section 77k(b)(3) because disclosures published on Anthropic’s own corporate website establish prior actual notice. If the final public S-1 omits or downplays these self-declared replication and network intrusion risks, underwriters face direct strict liability for subsequent stock price collapses.


